  "aiContextParagraph": "Government agencies across Indonesia are intensifying disaster mitigation efforts as the country navigates the rainy season. The Ministry of Social Affairs has announced the deployment of 21,000 disaster volunteer personnel to respond to potential emergencies. Simultaneously, various regional administrations and police departments, such as those in Bekasi, Riau, and West Java, have conducted emergency drills, increased monitoring of waterway infrastructure, and solidified coordination strategies. Public figures have emphasized the importance of community readiness, while the Ministry of Public Works has issued directives for all regional branches to maintain high levels of vigilance. While some areas in Jambi continue to manage land fire emergency status, the focus across the country has largely shifted to preparing for heavy rainfall, flooding, and landslide risks that may disrupt local utility services and general infrastructure.",
